WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.578
This is where the money lives, for the same synthetic family.

00:00:03.578 --> 00:00:08.211
The balance is what is owed between us, made only of costs we have both agreed.

00:00:08.211 --> 00:00:11.320
Beside it is what needs my OK, and what is coming up.

00:00:11.924 --> 00:00:13.548
Either parent logs a cost.

00:00:13.548 --> 00:00:18.734
Mia's school trip came to fourteen pounds fifty, I paid it, and we split it evenly.

00:00:18.734 --> 00:00:24.044
The summary says exactly what that means before I save it, and Sam is asked to agree.

00:00:24.648 --> 00:00:29.874
Sam disputed the birthday present I logged, and said why: it was a present from me.

00:00:29.874 --> 00:00:31.763
Sam's right, so I withdraw it.

00:00:31.763 --> 00:00:34.848
A disputed cost never counts towards the balance.

00:00:35.454 --> 00:00:36.533
This one matters.

00:00:36.533 --> 00:00:40.280
I open the football boots Sam logged, at forty-five pounds.

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:43.708
While I am reading, Sam changes the amount on a phone.

00:00:43.708 --> 00:00:48.534
When I agree, the app refuses: I would be agreeing to a version I never saw.

00:00:49.136 --> 00:00:50.847
It reloads with the new amount.

00:00:50.847 --> 00:00:53.496
Now I can see what I am agreeing to, so I agree.

00:00:55.188 --> 00:00:57.408
Paying back is one expense at a time.

00:00:57.408 --> 00:01:02.028
Sam says the uniform money is sent, and it is in my account, so I confirm it.

00:01:02.633 --> 00:01:04.448
Settle up does the rest at once.

00:01:04.448 --> 00:01:11.537
It lists every debt in both directions, nets them, and records the bank transfer that paid them, which has to add up exactly.

00:01:11.537 --> 00:01:14.033
It even writes the breakdown to send to Sam.

00:01:14.639 --> 00:01:17.799
I record it, and Sam confirms it arrived.

00:01:19.564 --> 00:01:20.355
Now I'm Sam.

00:01:20.355 --> 00:01:26.684
The same numbers, from the other side: the school trip to agree, and Alex's transfer to confirm.

00:01:27.289 --> 00:01:30.449
One tap agrees it, and it joins the balance for both of us.

00:01:31.759 --> 00:01:35.577
That was shared expenses in CoParent, from logging a cost to settling up.

00:01:35.577 --> 00:01:40.599
Every cost is agreed by both parents before it counts, so the balance is one both of them trust.
